Now test the DEGREE / quadratic-form structure of the best crossing count.
c3 is a quadratic form in tile bits (THM-554/HYP-2707). We test whether
the 'parallel crossing' count P (s1==s2) is ALSO a quadratic form, i.e.
P(bits) - P(0) is degree<=2 in bits, by finite differences.
   n=5: parallel-crossing 3rd-difference always 0? YES (deg<=2, QUADRATIC like c3)
   n=6: parallel-crossing 3rd-difference always 0? YES (deg<=2, QUADRATIC like c3)
